jp2z — third-party attribution
==============================

OpenJPEG (BSD-2-Clause)
-----------------------
jp2z contains code ported/translated from OpenJPEG (© its authors —
Université catholique de Louvain et al.; BSD-2-Clause) and links the OpenJPEG
binary as its Phase-1 decode backend. The full upstream license text and the
complete list of copyright holders are retained verbatim at:

    THIRD_PARTY/openjpeg-LICENSE.txt

OpenJPEG's role in jp2z:
  - build-time differential-test oracle (correctness reference), and
  - the Phase-1 runtime decode backend, linked as `libopenjp2` and retired
    by Phase 2 (pure-Zig decode).

The pure-Zig decode paths are a from-scratch reimplementation that references
OpenJPEG's algorithms under its permissive BSD-2-Clause terms. Should any jp2z
source file become a close translation of an OpenJPEG function, that file
carries a `// ported from openjpeg <file>, BSD-2-Clause` header in addition to
this NOTICE.

Upstream: https://github.com/uclouvain/openjpeg
